[29.131999, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[38;5;174m ▝▝   ▝▝ \u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;241m~/bare-app\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  Get to finished work sooner with\u001b[36GOpus\u001b[41G5.5.\u001b[46GSwitch\u001b[53Ganytime\u001b[61Gwith\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;105m/model\u001b[39m.\u001b[12G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;5;255m\u001b[38;5;248m❯ \u001b[38;5;16mFinance says our money rounding is wrong: div_cents() in \u001b[39m           \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;16mapp/money.py drops fractions of a cent, but amounts must round half\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;16mup (for example, 7% tax on 1050 cents must be 74 cents, not 73). \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;16mtests/te\u001b[12Gt_money.py pins the required behav\u001b[47Gour; you ca\u001b[60Grun it \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwith \u001b[38;5;105mpython3 -m pytest tests/test_money.py\u001b[38;5;16m.\u001b[47GFix i\u001b[53G and \u001b[59Gell me\u001b[66Gwhen\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bit\u001b[6Gis done. Do not commit;\u001b[30Gdo not pu\u001b[40Gh.\u001b[39m                          \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;16m●\u001b[39m I'll fix the rounding issue in the money module. Let me first check\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  the test requirements and current implementation.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;5;241mRead \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m files \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;16m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mNow\u001b[7GI\u001b[9Gcan\u001b[13Gsee\u001b[17Gthe\u001b[21Gissue.\u001b[28GThe\u001b[32Gtest\u001b[37Gexpects\u001b[45G\u001b[38;5;105mdiv_cents(7350, 100)\u001b[66G\u001b[39mto\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Breturn 74 (rounding\u001b[23G73.5\u001b[28Gup),\u001b[33Gbut\u001b[37Gthe\u001b[41Gcurrent\u001b[49Gimplementation\u001b[64Guses\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bfloor\u001b[9Gdivision\u001b[18Gwhich\u001b[24Greturns\u001b[32G73.\u001b[36GI\u001b[38Gneed\u001b[43Gto\u001b[46Gimplement\u001b[56Ghalf-up\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gr\u001b[5Gunding instead.\u001b[21G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u